hermal imaging assemblies, molded and diamond-turned infrared aspheric lenses, spherical lenses, and other optical components used in products that manipulate light; and infrared products, including catalog and custom infrared optics. The company also offers cooled and uncooled camera systems and modules for long range surveillance and detection, and engineering services. The company's products are used in defense products, border security, perimeter security, night vision systems, medical devices, laser aided industrial tools, automotive safety applications, telecommunications, machine vision and sensors, and other sectors. LightPath Technologies, Inc. was founded in 1985 and is headquartered in Orlando, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Shmuel  Rubin | President, CEO & Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $735,552 (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 414 people. Revenue per employee of $173K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 14%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["LightPath Technologies, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $363M market cap on $72M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +30% over the past three years and +15% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -25% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 37%.","The company is burning through $16M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -48.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 31.0% annua